:: Scene 1.3 Pt 2 {"position":"575,1200","size":"100,100"}
[WILLIAM
Oh look we're here.]

//Jack and William walk up to the counter where a woman is sitting//

[WILLIAM
Hi, one uniform for William please.]

[WOMAN
There's many Williams here can you be more specific.]

[WILLIAM
Bradford. William Bradford.]

//The woman types the name into the computer//

[WOMEN
Ah yes, it was supposed to be picked up last week. Let's see it should be around here somewhere.]

//The woman gets up and looks around the office for the uniform. She finds it and hands it to William//

[WOMEN
Here you go and next time try not to be late.]

[WILLIAM
Thank you and I'll try.]

//Jack and William walk back to their apartment//

[JACK
Why did you not come with me and Alyssa to pick up uniforms?]

[WILLIAM
I had to help my parents out. When we were in training they got laid off so they were low on money. They ended up selling the house and moving into a smaller one. I was helping them settle in since we had the weekend off.] 

[JACK
I'm so sorry man. I didn't mean to pry.]

[WILLIAM
Oh it's fine, I trust you.]

[JACK
You said your parents were laid off, what did they do?]

[WILLIAM
They worked at an engineering company out in the suburbs. They helped design some of the infrastruture there. Though because most funding for projects is given to the city the company didn't have enough money to pay all the staff.]

[JACK
Why isn't money given to the suburbs?]

[WILLIAM
Because the most important people live here. Out there people aren't as technically advanced or even thriving, and the only reason I know this is because I lived there.] 

[JACK
You're not from the city?]

[WILLIAM
I lived out in the suburbs. Luckily one of the better ones but so many are in a bad state. It's not what it used to be. The government makes sure those that live in the city are unaware of the outside towns and what happens within them. You know my parents were never big on time travel. They think it's done more harm than good. Which I don't blame them, there's been so many attacks outside the city that most people don't know about because the governent pushed them under a rug so people didn't panic.]

[JACK
I'm sorry man. Do you need any help?]

[WILLIAM
Please don't pity us Jack, my family is strong, we can overcome anything. Despite the circumstances my family is successful.]

[JACK
Ok sorry.]

[WILLIAM
It's ok, I understand you just care and want to help. I mentioned before I'm excited to help people, but I want to help everyone not just those that live here. Well it looks like we're back.]

//William and Jack arrive at the door to their apartment and open the door. Alyssa is putting the food on the table as they walk in.//

[ALYSSA
Hey just in time, foods ready. We have a big day tomorrow so we need to be in our best shape]

//Everyone sits down at the table and eats.//

[JACK
Thanks Alyssa.]

[WILLIAM
(says this with food in his mouth)
Yeah thanks, mhmm this is so good.

//The group falls into silence and finishes up their dinner. William goes to his room while Alyssa and Jack are cleaning up.//

[ALYSSA
Do you guys really think I don't deserve to be here? I thought we were a good team.]

[JACK
Hold on are you still upset by what William said?]

[ALYSSA
Possibly.]

[JACK
You know he was joking. If anyone deserved to be here it's you.]

[ALYSSA
Thanks you deserve it as well and sorry about what I said earlier.] 

[JACK
What do you mean?]

[ALYSSA
I meant not everyone is as lucky as you and can live out their dream.]

[JACK
Is this not what you want?]

[ALYSSA
Yes, no, I don't know! My father always wanted me to be a TPA agent. He said it can lead you to a successful future.]

[JACK
Don't you already have a successful future.]

[ALYSSA
Not in my father's eyes. He believes success is perfection and power. You know he was a TPA agent before he became Head of the Procedures and Policy Department for the TPA. Now he's trying to get me ready to take his place so he can be the head of the entire TPA. A lot of the time it's overwhelming and you guys are the only people that seem to genuinely care about me. Which is why I get upset when you think I don't deserve to be here because I do try.]

[JACK
I don't mean to pry but if you weren't a TPA Agent what would you want to do?]

[ALYSSA
I'm not sure, when I was little I wanted to be a doctor. But not the robot kind we have now. Like a person doctor. Father used to take me to the History Museum when I was little. He always said how important it is for us to advance and to have order so society may thrive. Though I would always spend the most time in the medical section. I don't know why, it just always interested me.]

[JACK
Well I guess I know who to go to if the robots shut down.]

[ALYSSA
I don't know about that. I'm not a trained professional.]

[JACK
I'm sure with enough practice you'd figure it out. Besides it's not to late to try something new.]

[ALYSSA
Yeah I suppose so. I just don't want to let him down. He has worked so hard and because of that he's now in the position he's in. My mother tried to give me a normal life but after she died my father became so focused on keeping up the legacy. I think it's because I was the only part of her left and he wanted her to be remembered for her greatness.]

[JACK
Oh I'm so sorry, I didn't know.]

[ALYSSA
Why would you. Besides it happened when I was really young. I can barely remember her. Anyways after she died, father started training me to get into the TPA program. And as you can see he was successful.]

[ALYSSA
(Feeder Line)
I know that was a lot. Sorry for dumping all that on you.]

[JACK
[[You do belong.]]
[[You don't belong.]]
[[It was a lot.]]
